  "origin": "topic-postpone (design/topic-postpone.md R12) gave an approved gap candidate the same durable brief a harvested topic has. Before it, the candidate's whole substance was a summary and a description on the map row over an analysis file the next run overwrites, so a topic picked up months later opened on a paragraph. Nothing covered the write: the sibling gate case walks the approve/skip pair and stops at the map row. This pins the brief's shape, the pointer riding the add rather than a follow-up field write, and the sweep's second commit — the state scope does not reach discovery/briefs, and an uncommitted brief is the failure the extra commit exists to prevent",
